315
00:28:07,600 --> 00:28:10,700
The system can 't provide that for her , I think that I can .

316
00:28:10,900 --> 00:28:13,600
Better than anyone , given my training .

317
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:16,500
We spend so much of our time negotiating red tape ,

318
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:20,800
I think if we look at this situation , this one situation ,

319
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:24,900
this one child , it 's clear what 's best for her .

320
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:32,900
How long till Foster Services can place her in a permanent home ?

321
00:28:33,300 --> 00:28:36,500
Three weeks , three months , it 's hard to predict .

322
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:51,500
No more visits .

323
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:55,000
- What ? - They said yes .

324
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:01,400
It 's your new beginning .

325
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Okay . It 's what I like to think of as a glass-half-full situation .

326
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:14,300
Bathroom . Kitchen . Fish .

327
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:17,700
And this is your room .

328
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:23,100
Be okay ?

329
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:34,200
- You live alone ? - Just me .

330
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:37,000
Just us .

331
00:29:43,100 --> 00:29:44,082
What 's this ?

332
00:29:44,108 --> 00:29:45,825
It 's chamomile .

333
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,500
Helps me sleep .

334
00:29:52,100 --> 00:29:55,200
You know none of this should ever have happened .

335
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:57,700
If I could make it go away , I would .

336
