How sick is that ?

382
00:34:24,400 --> 00:34:26,300
Well , fear and hatred are part of the same pathology .

383
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:28,200
- See you . Bye , Diego . - You too , Lily .

384
00:34:28,300 --> 00:34:29,800
- But I forgot . - Bye .

385
00:34:30,100 --> 00:34:32,100
- Bye . - You don 't think they 're crazy .

386
00:34:32,300 --> 00:34:34,300
Well , I 'm coming around .

387
00:34:40,500 --> 00:34:43,300
- I love you . - Love you , too .

388
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:52,500
- Wayne 's looking for you . - Okay .

389
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:57,516
Wayne wants to see you .

390
00:34:57,542 --> 00:34:58,925
Yeah , I got it .

391
00:35:06,500 --> 00:35:08,400
What 's up with Diego ?

392
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:09,420
Oh , hey .

393
00:35:09,446 --> 00:35:12,725
Look , why don 't we go talk in my office .

394
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:15,100
No , tell me what 's going on .

395
00:35:16,700 --> 00:35:17,900
Well , we don 't ...

396
00:35:17,926 --> 00:35:22,725
.. We don 't know why yet but he killed both his parents last night .

397
00:35:29,500 --> 00:35:30,704
Excuse me ... Go ahead .

398
00:35:30,730 --> 00:35:32,425
Officer , let her through .

399
00:35:36,100 --> 00:35:37,200
What happened ?

400
00:35:37,400 --> 00:35:40,500
Gets a tyre iron from the garage , comes back inside ,

401
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:48,400
locks all the doors and windows , and kills them in their sleep .

402
00:35:54,700 --> 00:35:57,100
" Slaughters " would be a better word .

403
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,900
Oh , my God !

404
00:36:21,100 --> 00:36:24,000
A 10-year-old did this ? There 's no way .

405
00:36:24,300 --> 00:36:26,016
I was there when they brought him in .

406
00:36:26,042 --> 00:36:27,525
Took three guys to subdue him .

407
00:36:27,800 --> 00:36:29,700
And the kid was climbing the walls .

408
00:36:31,500 --> 00:36:33,100
Man 's best friend , huh ?

409
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:53,558
What happened ?

410
00:36:53,584 --> 00:36:55,225
Tell me what happened .

411
00:36:55,500 --> 00:36:57,400
I killed my mom and dad .

412
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:07,600
Every family you sit down with ,

413
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:11,000
every day of every week , it 's a family in crisis .

414
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:12,688
Those are your odds .

415
00:37:12,714 --> 00:37:15,325
Well , that 's your job , trying to beat them .

416
00:37:20,600 --> 00:37:22,300
You 're one person , Em .

417
00:37:23,100 --> 00:37:25,100
You can 't save the world .

418
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:31,600
I know somebody you did save .

419
00:37:35,300 --> 00:37:36,300
Yeah .

420
00:37:39,300 --> 00:37:42,000
- You okay ? - Yeah .

421
00:37:42,700 --> 00:37:44,800
It 's just work . Don 't worry .

422
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:49,800
- I think you have a hard job . - So do I.

423
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:55,200
People have kids and then they decide they don 't want to be parents .

424
00:37:55,400 --> 00:37:58,900
And then the kids grow up thinking it 's their fault .

425
00:38:00,800 --> 00:38:02,900
Is that what your parents did ?

426
00:38:04,700 --> 00:38:06,600
You said you were alone .

427
00:38:08,700 --> 00:38:09,700
Yeah .

428
00:38:11,800 --> 00:38:13,700
I never met my dad .

429
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:18,600
And my mom ... My mom had problems .

430
00:38:19,200 --> 00:38:20,720
She must have scared you .

431
00:38:20,746 --> 00:38:22,325
Why do you say that ?

432
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:25,900
You don 't like to talk about it .

433
00:38:28,700 --> 00:38:30,700
You 're a clever little girl .

434
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:44,200
Sweetheart .

435
00:38:44,226 --> 00:38:45,625
Breakfast .

436
00:38:48,400 --> 00:38:49,700
What you got ?

437
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,500
Let me see .

438
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:09,800
You went through my things ?

439
00:39:11,700 --> 00:39:12,779
I 'm sorry .

440
00:39:12,805 --> 00:39:15,825
I wanted to know about you .

441
00:39:24,600 --> 00:39:26,500
Is that your mother ?

442
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:31,100
What happened to her ?

443
00:39:32,700 --> 00:39:35,700
She died when I was about your age .

444
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:40,700
- How ? - An accident .

445
00:39:47,200 --> 00:39:50,700
It was raining and she was driving too fast .

446
00:39:53,400 --> 00:39:55,100
We had an accident .

447
00:39:58,500 --> 00:40:00,200
Are you mad at me ?

448
00:40:02,600 --> 00:40:04,300
No , I 'm not mad at you .

449
00:40:05,400 --> 00:40:07,300
But I need you not to do that again , okay ?

450
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:10,200
Go through my private things without asking .

451
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:14,100
Okay ? All right .

452
00:40:15,700 --> 00:40:17,216
Omelette 's getting cold .

453
00:40:17,242 --> 00:40:18,125
Better hurry .

454
00:40:33,300 --> 00:40:37,100
You watch , six months , their lawyer will hire an expert

455
00:40:37,300 --> 00:40:40,800
to say they 're rehabbed and they 'll sue for custody when they get out .

456
00:40:41,100 --> 00:40:42,600
She 's not going back there .

457
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:45,500
I 'll take her out of the state before I let them near her again .

458
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,600
Didn 't hear you say that .

459
00:40:49,500 --> 00:40:50,800
You guys okay ?

460
00:40:53,100 --> 00:40:57,300
We 're great . She 's sweet , very intuitive about everything .

461
00:41:02,100 --> 00:41:04,400
You wanted to talk about something ?

462
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:07,000
We pulled the Ramirezes ' phone records .

463
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:09,500
There was a call that night before the murder .

464
00:41:09,700 --> 00:41:10,300
From who ?

465
00:41:10,326 --> 00:41:12,725
The call came from your house , Emily .

466
00:41:13,700 --> 00:41:14,600
What ?

467
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:17,900
I 'm not accusing you of anything , I just want to know what was said .

468
00:41:18,100 --> 00:41:19,800
But that 's impossible .

469
00:41:20,100 --> 00:41:22,300
I mean , I might have called them the week before or something , but I ...

470
00:41:22,500 --> 00:41:25,500
I 'm talking to you as a friend , you know that , right ?

471
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:27,700
Mike , did you not hear me ?

472
00:41:27,900 --> 00:41:31,500
As a friend , I 'm telling you that I didn 't call that family .

473
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:38,553
He 's in my group .

474
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:42,125
Why , did something happen ?

475
00:41:45,200 --> 00:41:47,100
We 're trying to figure out why .

476
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:50,200
Diego got a call from here , last Thursday night .

477
00:41:50,400 --> 00:41:52,400
I 'm just wondering if he might have said something .

478
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:53,515
That wasn 't me .

479
00:41:53,541 --> 00:41:55,125
You didn 't call him ?

480
00:41:57,100 --> 00:42:00,500
Lily , it 's difficult sometimes to tell the truth ,

481
00:42:00,900 --> 00:42:03,000
but I know you will because you 're a good kid .

482
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:05,000
I am telling the truth .

483
00:42:05,900 --> 00:42:07,926
My backup files are in the cabinet .

484
00:42:07,952 --> 00:42:09,225
Diego 's is in there .

485
00:42:09,900 --> 00:42:14,500
Maybe you got curious and went through some , dialled a number ?

486
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:17,100
It wasn 't me , I swear .

487
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:19,924
The call came at 2 : 00 a.m.

488
00:42:19,950 --> 00:42:21,725
You ever up that late ?

489
00:42:21,900 --> 00:42:22,957
I didn 't call him .

490
00:42:22,983 --> 00:42:24,625
You ever up that late ?

491
00:42:24,800 --> 00:42:25,844
Mike , she said no .

492
00:42:25,870 --> 00:42:27,725
Maybe somebody made a mistake .

493
00:42:29,300 --> 00:42:30,700
Yeah , maybe so .

494
00:42:37,700 --> 00:42:39,488
Why would Diego do this ?

495
00:42:39,514 --> 00:42:41,525
He loved his mom and dad .

496
00:42:43,300 --> 00:42:46,700
You never want to think anyone you know is capable of that kind of thing .

497
00:42:47,100 --> 00:42:50,600
In your mind , it 's always some nameless , faceless creature .

498
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:55,000
Sometimes , the city seems full of them .

499
00:42:55,900 --> 00:42:58,600
But they 're just people , like you and me .

500
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:03,000
She 's lying .

501
00:43:09,700 --> 00:43:11,300
Do you believe me ?

502
00:43:12,700 --> 00:43:14,100
I believe you .

503
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:22,100
I need to ask you something about the night it happened .

504
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:24,122
Did you get a call ?

505
00:43:24,148 --> 00:43:25,325
Really late ?

506
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:30,300
You didn 't .

507
00:43:32,200 --> 00:43:34,100
Diego , I know that you did .

508
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:38,400
The call came from my house .

509
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,600
What 's the matter ?

510
00:43:45,700 --> 00:43:48,100
What 's scaring you ? Diego .

511
00:43:49,800 --> 00:43:50,895
